.backups/

# Claude Code tooling artifacts — local state, not for version control.
#
# NOTE THE `/*` RATHER THAN `/`. Git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY, so with
# `.claude/` the negations below would never be consulted and the hook scripts would stay
# invisible. Ignoring the CONTENTS instead lets specific paths be re-included.
.claude/*

# ...EXCEPT the parts that are project policy rather than local state.
#
# settings.json holds the shared permission list and the HOOK WIRING. The hook scripts are
# the commit gate: secrets, .env, vendor names, post-edit tsc. A commit gate that is not
# committed protects one laptop and nothing else, which is the same as no gate at all for
# every other machine and for anyone reviewing this repo.
#
# settings.local.json stays ignored on purpose. It accumulates per-machine permission
# grants and is genuinely local state.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
